The first code-level distinction is now clear: `state.py` does not recompute or overwrite survival; it serializes whatever `ForecastObservation.survival` it is handed. The stored pilot rows were produced by the primitive fallback’s geometric/legal predicate, while the exact target replay uses the coupled evaluator’s served-set predicate. I’m next pinning down the smallest pre-decision scalars that separate each witness and can actually be supplied by named production functions.
