Feature declaration, before measurement:

- C1 variant (one scalar only): `predecision_network_max_rf_over_cap = max RF power already present in the committed network / 1.65 W`. It is derived from the current base-state evaluation, never from the focal candidate evaluation. For the constructed witness it is `0.8/1.65` versus `1.5/1.65`.
- C2: no admissible feature variant. The two real rows have the same physical decision-time tape, committed mapping, incumbent mapping, and focal candidate action; their exact targets diverge only because the target projection compares against different future carrier transitions. Encoding that carrier/future result would violate the stated admissibility rule.

I’m freezing those choices now and will report the C2 “after” score unchanged, rather than tune around the result.
