Measurement is complete: the declared C1 scalar is exactly `1.0` for all 30 corpus anchors (the current network is cap-saturated), so it changes neither neighbor selection nor held-out metrics. This is the clean negative result the diagnostic was designed to expose. I’m writing the report now, including the adapter-vs-serializer distinction and the sealed-lineage stop condition.
